sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh faithfully reproduces Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph) morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-hox-turing-polydactyly-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py; output: docs/media/hox_turing_polydactyly_comparison.png; organism: Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/58b898c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: df2380b6b9d39cc7343d21970d756072ccaee92ea4d1cd0e08f469c328909c2c; artifact_sha256: 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/hox_turing_polydactyly_reference.json=06c60968ccdce3a7..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/pass3_aer_growth_reference.json=311a1e81311eabab..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/scout_manifest.json=c0608869f6d213a4..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/vertebrate_autopod_digits_specimen.jpg=995e43a2a0cf7815...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-hox-turing-polydactyly-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sheth et al. (2012): progressive loss of distal Hox (Hoxa13, Hoxd11-13) in a Gli3-null background shrinks the digit period (wavelength) of a Turing-type mechanism, raising digit number from 5 to ~14 at roughly constant autopod width (Figs. 1-3) | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain the reaction-diffusion equations acquire an advection term and a dilution term -(div v) u; patterns lag the fixed-domain wavelength and transition by peak insertion / frequency doubling | Boehm et al. (2010): limb bud proliferation is distally biased but a proliferation gradient alone is insufficient to explain bud shape | Summerbell (1974): AER excision arrests distal outgrowth; the earlier the excision the more proximal the truncation; reconstructed_in_script: Sheth et al. (2012) linear dispersion, k_c(H) and the cubic-saturated two-component PDE on a 1D Neumann arc and a 2D fixed-width polar fan (Pass 2), plus the Pass 3 AER-FGF8 kinematic growing fan in ALE form with dilution, mesh-relative advection, physical-metric angular modes, backward-Euler radial diffusion, Lagrangian tracers, AER regression and ablation, a g_max sweep and the quasi-static digit-number/width law; 6-genotype allelic series; dual negative controls; radiograph digit-ray segmentation; 5 Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: Growth is kinematic: g(r,t) is prescribed by the mitogen field and div v = g; no elastic/viscous constitutive law, stress balance or oriented cell behaviour is solved (Boehm et al. 2010 show these matter for shape) | Digit-ray (stripe) orientation is imposed by PD/AP diffusion anisotropy D_r = 0.05 D rather than derived from the Fgf/Wnt proximodistal modulation of Raspopovic et al. (2014) | k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and g_u(H) = 200 f_u + 25 k_c^4 - 4.5|tr J_kc| are closure ansaetze that interpolate the allelic series and pin sigma_max ~ 4.5; they are not fitted to Sheth et al.'s supplementary parameter values | The 1D arc and fixed-width fan solvers seed the target cosine mode (-0.08 cos(n_target s)); only the Pass 3 growing fan evolves from seeded noise alone, and it shows a growth-induced wavelength lag (N_grow = 3.5 WT, 13.0 null vs law 5 / 14); does_not_claim: 3D limb bud geometry, cell-level mechanics, Sox9/Bmp/Wnt three-node kinetics, quantitative reproduction of Sheth et al.'s Fig. 2G digit-period measurements (not vendored), or hour-calibrated developmental time]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.913"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "58b898c" .
}

